meta {
  name: Authorize Space Sync (space.authorizeSpaceSync)
  type: http
  seq: 141
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.authorizeSpaceSync
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://did:plc:exampleauthority/space/org.example.bucket/self",
    "credentialKey": "{{credentialKey}}",
    "delegationToken": "{{delegationToken}}",
    "clientAttestation": "{{clientAttestation}}"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
  credentialKey: <the client's P-256 did:key (did:key:zDn…) — becomes the credential's cnf.kid>
  delegationToken: <token from getDelegationToken on the user's PDS — omit the field for a publicRead memberspace>
  clientAttestation: <ES256 atproto-client-attestation+jwt signed by a key in the client's metadata JWKS: iss = sub = client_id, aud {authorityDid}#atproto_pds, fresh iat/exp, single-use jti — omit the field unless the space gates on the app>
}

docs {
  Atproto Spaces (proposal 0016). Called on the space authority's PDS, with no request
  authorization: mints a 10 min space credential (`typ atproto-space-credential+jwt`, `kid
  #atproto`, no `aud`, `cnf.kid` = `credentialKey`) and returns it with the space's current
  `spaceRev` (omitted before the space's first update). The credential is then presented as
  `Authorization: Atproto-Space-Credential <credential>` with an `Atproto-Space-Audience`
  header (the repo owner's DID on a repo read, the authority's on a space-level one) and an
  RFC 9421 signature tagged `atproto-space-credential` covering both, by the `credentialKey`.

  `delegationToken` names the account (its `aud` is `{authorityDid}#atproto_pds`); without
  one, only a `publicRead` memberspace mints. `clientAttestation` is verified whenever present:
  `client_id` (its `iss`/`sub`) is resolved to its client-metadata document and the JWKS that
  document publishes, and the `jti` is spent single-use. The attested client_id is what
  memberspace's `allowedApps` is matched against, and what is forwarded to a managing app's
  `checkAccess`. The lexicon's `notify` is not read yet.

  Errors (lexicon names, all HTTP 400): InvalidRequest (credentialKey not a P-256 did:key),
  SpaceNotFound (unknown, or not anchored on an account here), RepoTakendown / RepoDeactivated
  (the authority's account), SpaceDeleted, InvalidDelegationToken (bad
  signature/typ/kid/sub/aud/exp, or already used), InvalidClientAttestation (malformed,
  unresolvable client_id, wrong signature/aud, expired, or replayed), AppNotAuthorized (no
  attestation, or a client_id not on `allowedApps`), AccountNotAuthorized (refused on the
  account: not a reading member, no delegation token on a space that is not publicRead, or a
  managing app that answered no or could not be reached).
}
